# Sleigh specification for the Ricoh 2A03 (the NES/Famicom CPU), language id 6502:LE:16:2a03
# (grm-yvmw). The 2A03 is a 6502 core with the decimal mode disconnected: SED/CLD still
# set and clear D, but ADC/SBC always take the binary path. Only the documented opcode set is
# decoded, so decoding is identical to stock Ghidra's 6502:LE:16:default; what differs is
# the corrected ADC/SBC p-code of 6502core.sinc (grm-o9k, grm-ef46).
#
# NO_DECIMAL compiles the D branch of adcNmos/sbcNmos out of 6502core.sinc, rather than
# keeping a copied core.

@define NO_DECIMAL "1"

@include "6502core.sinc"
